1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,241
A nebula is a giant cloud of dust and gas, mostly hydrogen. Some, like the Orion Nebula,

2
00:00:05,241 --> 00:00:11,600
are stellar nurseries where stars are born; others, like the Crab Nebula, are the remains of exploded stars.

3
00:00:12,659 --> 00:00:17,605
In a stellar nursery, dust and gas form a clump whose gravity pulls in more matter.

4
00:00:17,605 --> 00:00:23,081
It collapses and heats up, until particles in the core react and a new star begins to shine.

5
00:00:23,081 --> 00:00:25,260
Stars can live for billions of years!

6
00:00:26,319 --> 00:00:31,736
Nebulae are not just pictures in a book. Here are four real examples that astronomers study.

7
00:00:32,795 --> 00:00:39,036
On a dark night you can see the Orion Nebula without a telescope, as a fuzzy patch in the sword of Orion.

8
00:00:39,036 --> 00:00:41,568
Inside it, new stars are forming right now.

9
00:00:42,627 --> 00:00:47,220
The Pillars of Creation are huge columns of dust and gas in the Eagle Nebula.

10
00:00:47,220 --> 00:00:51,165
Space telescopes have photographed young stars forming inside them.

11
00:00:52,224 --> 00:00:53,991
The Crab Nebula is different.

12
00:00:53,991 --> 00:01:00,232
It is the remains of a star that exploded, and the explosion was recorded by astronomers in the year 1054.

13
00:01:01,291 --> 00:01:07,474
Our own Sun formed in the same way, from a collapsing cloud of gas and dust, about 4.6 billion years ago.

14
00:01:08,533 --> 00:01:13,479
So some nebulae are where stars are born, and some are what is left when stars die.

15
00:01:13,479 --> 00:01:18,543
Pause and decide: what force makes a clump of gas in a nebula collapse to form a star?

16
00:01:19,602 --> 00:01:25,078
Now it is your turn to shine! Pause the video after each question and try to answer it first.

17
00:01:26,137 --> 00:01:29,905
Question 1: Where are most asteroids found? Pause the video now.

18
00:01:30,964 --> 00:01:34,144
Answer: In the asteroid belt between Mars and Jupiter.

19
00:01:35,203 --> 00:01:40,031
Question 2: Why did an asteroid impact cause mass extinction? Pause the video now.

20
00:01:41,090 --> 00:01:44,800
Answer: Dust blocked sunlight, so plants died and Earth cooled.

21
00:01:45,859 --> 00:01:49,509
Question 3: What is the collision theory? Pause the video now.

22
00:01:50,568 --> 00:01:54,749
Answer: The Moon formed when a planet called Theia hit the young Earth.

23
00:01:55,808 --> 00:01:58,752
Question 4: What is a nebula? Pause the video now.

24
00:01:59,811 --> 00:02:03,285
Answer: A giant cloud of dust and gas where stars can form.
